  "text": "NEW ZEALAND\nNEW ZEALAND GOVERNMENT OFFICE,\nMELBOURNE.\n9th June, 1955.\nC. E. McFadyen, Esq.,\nSecretary,\nDepartment of Shipping\nand Transport,\n497 Collins Street,\nMELBOURNE.\nDear Mr.\ntuckadyen\nwas very pleased to see the\nannouncement in this morning's paper of\nthe honour conferred on you by Her\nMajesty the Queen, and would like to offer\nmy sincerest congraulations on this well-\ndeserved recognition of your good work.\nPluck!\nNEW ZEAL\nND TRADE COMMISSIONER.\n19,\nTHE CATHEGRAL\nCOLOGNE 1919\nvy.o.\n20 A.C.C.S.\nTRAJOR MOLELLADO, PIRARME\n• COLONEL CLATTOr\nIN THE SMON, SARS POTERIES\n1919",
